From: Jetha Chan <jetha@splatterfacegames.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: s5kc505a: accept the read-only timing controls

A mode change updates HBLANK through __v4l2_ctrl_modify_range(), which
calls s_ctrl. If the sensor is still runtime active (within the 1 s
autosuspend delay after a stream), s_ctrl reached the default case and
returned -EINVAL, so VIDIOC_SUBDEV_S_FMT failed after the mode had
already been switched, and the VBLANK and EXPOSURE ranges were left at
the old mode's values. Treat HBLANK, PIXEL_RATE and LINK_FREQ as no-ops
in s_ctrl.

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/s5kc505a.c b/drivers/media/i2c/s5kc505a.c
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/s5kc505a.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/s5kc505a.c
@@ -547,6 +547,15 @@
 		ret = cci_write(s5kc505a->regmap, S5KC505A_REG_TEST_PATTERN,
 				ctrl->val, NULL);
 		break;
+	case V4L2_CID_HBLANK:
+	case V4L2_CID_PIXEL_RATE:
+	case V4L2_CID_LINK_FREQ:
+		/*
+		 * Read-only, follow the mode; set_pad_format updates them
+		 * and can do so while the sensor is still runtime active.
+		 */
+		ret = 0;
+		break;
 	default:
 		ret = -EINVAL;
 		break;
